        "# Activity 1: Multiple Linear Regression Worksheet\n",
        "**Unit I \u2013 Regression Foundations & Linear Regression**\n",
        "\n",
        "## 1. Objective & Problem Statement\n",
        "**Objective:** To understand how multiple input variables together explain a continuous target, fit a Multiple Linear Regression model manually (on a small sample) and programmatically, compare it against a single-feature baseline, interpret coefficients and intercept, check regression assumptions (including multicollinearity), and evaluate performance on unseen test data.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Problem Statement:** Given advertising expenditure across three media channels (`TV`, `Radio`, and `Newspaper`, in thousands of USD), predict product `Sales` (in thousands of units) using Multiple Linear Regression, verify manual normal-equation calculations against a library implementation, and assess whether adding `Radio` and `Newspaper` improves predictive accuracy over `TV` alone.\n",
        "\n",
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 2. Environment Setup & Dataset Loading\n",
        "**Dataset:** Advertising Dataset (200 market observations)  \n",
        "**Original Source:** *An Introduction to Statistical Learning* (James, Witten, Hastie, Tibshirani) \u2014 [Advertising.csv](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/justmarkham/scikit-learn-videos/master/data/Advertising.csv)"
      ],
      "id": "cell-01-87f5ba88"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 1,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Python: 3.11.2 | NumPy: 2.1.3 | Pandas: 2.2.3\n",
            "Raw dataset shape: (200, 5)\n",
            "   Unnamed: 0     TV  Radio  Newspaper  Sales\n",
            "0           1  230.1   37.8       69.2   22.1\n",
            "1           2   44.5   39.3       45.1   10.4\n",
            "2           3   17.2   45.9       69.3    9.3\n",
            "3           4  151.5   41.3       58.5   18.5\n",
            "4           5  180.8   10.8       58.4   12.9\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
