    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 5. Manual Calculation Worksheet (6 Observations, 2 Features: TV & Radio)\n",
        "We select the first 6 observations from the dataset and solve the Ordinary Least Squares normal equations $(\\mathbf{X}^T \\mathbf{X})\\mathbf{b} = \\mathbf{X}^T \\mathbf{y}$ step by step."
      ],
      "id": "cell-08-9a7a8132"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 5,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Selected 6-Observation Sample:\n",
            "       TV  Radio  Sales\n",
            "0  230.1   37.8   22.1\n",
            "1   44.5   39.3   10.4\n",
            "2   17.2   45.9    9.3\n",
            "3  151.5   41.3   18.5\n",
            "4  180.8   10.8   12.9\n",
            "5    8.7   48.9    7.2\n",
            "\n",
            "Design Matrix X (6x3):\n",
            "[[  1.  230.1  37.8]\n",
            " [  1.   44.5  39.3]\n",
            " [  1.   17.2  45.9]\n",
            " [  1.  151.5  41.3]\n",
            " [  1.  180.8  10.8]\n",
            " [  1.    8.7  48.9]]\n",
            "\n",
            "Target Vector y (6x1):\n",
            "[22.1 10.4  9.3 18.5 12.9  7.2]\n",
            "\n",
            "X^T X:\n",
            "[[6.0000000e+00 6.3280000e+02 2.2400000e+02]\n",
            " [6.3280000e+02 1.1093868e+05 1.9871130e+04]\n",
            " [2.2400000e+02 1.9871130e+04 9.2936800e+03]]\n",
            "\n",
            "X^T y:\n",
            "[   80.4  10905.68  2926.42]\n",
            "\n",
            "(X^T X)^(-1):\n",
            "[[ 3.91793415e+00 -8.80631000e-03 -7.56025500e-02]\n",
            " [-8.80631000e-03  3.44000000e-05  1.38700000e-04]\n",
            " [-7.56025500e-02  1.38700000e-04  1.63325000e-03]]\n",
            "\n",
            "Solved Manual Coefficients: b0 = -2.281725, b1 (TV) = 0.073039, b2 (Radio) = 0.213710\n",
            "\n",
            "Observation 1 Actual Sales = 22.1000\n",
            "Observation 1 Predicted Sales = 22.602884\n",
            "Observation 1 Residual (y - y_hat) = -0.502884\n",
            "\n",
            "Library lstsq Verification: b0 = -2.281725, b1 = 0.073039, b2 = 0.213710\n",
            "Max absolute difference: 8.26e-14\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "sample = df.iloc[:6][[\"TV\", \"Radio\", \"Sales\"]].copy()\n",
        "print(\"Selected 6-Observation Sample:\\n\", sample.to_string())\n",
        "\n",
        "X_man = np.column_stack([np.ones(len(sample)), sample[\"TV\"].values, sample[\"Radio\"].values])\n",
        "y_man = sample[\"Sales\"].values\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nDesign Matrix X (6x3):\")\n",
        "print(X_man)\n",
        "print(\"\\nTarget Vector y (6x1):\")\n",
        "print(y_man)\n",
        "\n",
        "XtX = X_man.T @ X_man\n",
        "Xty = X_man.T @ y_man\n",
        "print(\"\\nX^T X:\")\n",
        "print(np.round(XtX, 4))\n",
        "print(\"\\nX^T y:\")\n",
        "print(np.round(Xty, 4))\n",
        "\n",
        "XtX_inv = np.linalg.inv(XtX)\n",
        "b_man = XtX_inv @ Xty\n",
        "print(\"\\n(X^T X)^(-1):\")\n",
        "print(np.round(XtX_inv, 8))\n",
        "print(f\"\\nSolved Manual Coefficients: b0 = {b_man[0]:.6f}, b1 (TV) = {b_man[1]:.6f}, b2 (Radio) = {b_man[2]:.6f}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Predict for observation 1 (index 0) and compute residual\n",
        "y_hat_obs1 = b_man[0] + b_man[1] * X_man[0, 1] + b_man[2] * X_man[0, 2]\n",
        "res_obs1 = y_man[0] - y_hat_obs1\n",
        "print(f\"\\nObservation 1 Actual Sales = {y_man[0]:.4f}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Observation 1 Predicted Sales = {y_hat_obs1:.6f}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Observation 1 Residual (y - y_hat) = {res_obs1:.6f}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Verify with numpy.linalg.lstsq\n",
        "b_lib_sample, _, _, _ = np.linalg.lstsq(X_man, y_man, rcond=None)\n",
        "print(f\"\\nLibrary lstsq Verification: b0 = {b_lib_sample[0]:.6f}, b1 = {b_lib_sample[1]:.6f}, b2 = {b_lib_sample[2]:.6f}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Max absolute difference: {np.max(np.abs(b_man - b_lib_sample)):.2e}\")"
      ],
      "id": "cell-09-e109db3f"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 6. Train-Test Split (80:20) & Baseline vs. Multiple Linear Regression\n",
        "We split the 200 observations into 160 training records (80%) and 40 test records (20%) with `random_state=42`. We fit:\n",
        "1. **Single-Feature Baseline:** `Sales ~ TV` (strongest predictor, $r = 0.7822$).\n",
        "2. **Multiple Linear Regression:** `Sales ~ TV + Radio + Newspaper`.\n",
        "3. **Standardized Multiple Linear Regression:** Fitted using training-set mean and standard deviation only (no data leakage) to compare relative feature influence."
      ],
      "id": "cell-10-c2424d4d"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 6,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Train observations: 160 | Test observations: 40\n",
            "\n",
            "Single-Feature Model: Sales = 6.9177 + 0.046973 * TV\n",
            "Single-Feature Test Metrics: {'MAE': np.float64(2.92), 'MSE': np.float64(13.5526), 'RMSE': np.float64(3.6814), 'R2': np.float64(0.4947), 'Adj_R2': np.float64(0.4814)}\n",
            "\n",
            "Multiple Linear Regression: Sales = 3.0389 + 0.046363*TV + 0.175484*Radio + 0.001084*Newspaper\n",
            "Multiple Model Test Metrics: {'MAE': np.float64(1.2575), 'MSE': np.float64(2.5304), 'RMSE': np.float64(1.5907), 'R2': np.float64(0.9056), 'Adj_R2': np.float64(0.8978)}\n",
            "\n",
            "Standardized Coefficients (relative influence, training data only):\n",
            "  TV        : Raw = +0.046363 | Standardized = +3.9377\n",
            "  Radio     : Raw = +0.175484 | Standardized = +2.6197\n",
            "  Newspaper : Raw = +0.001084 | Standardized = +0.0231\n",
            "\n",
            "Model Comparison Table (Test Set):\n",
            "                          Model    MAE     MSE   RMSE     R2  Adj_R2\n",
            "            Single-Feature (TV) 2.9200 13.5526 3.6814 0.4947  0.4814\n",
            "Multiple (TV, Radio, Newspaper) 1.2575  2.5304 1.5907 0.9056  0.8978\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "indices = np.arange(len(df))\n",
        "rng = np.random.default_rng(RANDOM_STATE)\n",
        "shuffled_idx = rng.permutation(indices)\n",
        "split_point = int(0.8 * len(df))\n",
        "train_idx, test_idx = shuffled_idx[:split_point], shuffled_idx[split_point:]\n",
        "\n",
        "train_df = df.iloc[train_idx].reset_index(drop=True)\n",
        "test_df = df.iloc[test_idx].reset_index(drop=True)\n",
        "print(f\"Train observations: {len(train_df)} | Test observations: {len(test_df)}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "def fit_ols(X, y):\n",
        "    X_design = np.column_stack([np.ones(len(X)), X])\n",
        "    beta, _, _, _ = np.linalg.lstsq(X_design, y, rcond=None)\n",
        "    return beta[0], beta[1:]\n",
        "\n",
        "def predict_ols(X, intercept, coefs):\n",
        "    return intercept + X @ coefs\n",
        "\n",
        "def regression_metrics(y_true, y_pred, p):\n",
        "    n = len(y_true)\n",
        "    residuals = y_true - y_pred\n",
        "    mae = np.mean(np.abs(residuals))\n",
        "    mse = np.mean(residuals ** 2)\n",
        "    rmse = np.sqrt(mse)\n",
        "    ss_res = np.sum(residuals ** 2)\n",
        "    ss_tot = np.sum((y_true - np.mean(y_true)) ** 2)\n",
        "    r2 = 1.0 - ss_res / ss_tot\n",
        "    adj_r2 = 1.0 - (1.0 - r2) * (n - 1) / (n - p - 1)\n",
        "    return {\"MAE\": mae, \"MSE\": mse, \"RMSE\": rmse, \"R2\": r2, \"Adj_R2\": adj_r2}\n",
        "\n",
        "# 1. Single-feature baseline (TV)\n",
        "X_train_1 = train_df[[\"TV\"]].values\n",
        "X_test_1 = test_df[[\"TV\"]].values\n",
        "y_train = train_df[\"Sales\"].values\n",
        "y_test = test_df[\"Sales\"].values\n",
        "\n",
        "b0_single, b_single = fit_ols(X_train_1, y_train)\n",
        "y_pred_test_1 = predict_ols(X_test_1, b0_single, b_single)\n",
        "metrics_1 = regression_metrics(y_test, y_pred_test_1, p=1)\n",
        "print(f\"\\nSingle-Feature Model: Sales = {b0_single:.4f} + {b_single[0]:.6f} * TV\")\n",
        "print(\"Single-Feature Test Metrics:\", {k: round(v, 4) for k, v in metrics_1.items()})\n",
        "\n",
        "# 2. Multiple Linear Regression (TV, Radio, Newspaper)\n",
        "X_train_m = train_df[features].values\n",
        "X_test_m = test_df[features].values\n",
        "\n",
        "b0_mult, b_mult = fit_ols(X_train_m, y_train)\n",
        "y_pred_test_m = predict_ols(X_test_m, b0_mult, b_mult)\n",
        "metrics_m = regression_metrics(y_test, y_pred_test_m, p=3)\n",
        "print(f\"\\nMultiple Linear Regression: Sales = {b0_mult:.4f} + {b_mult[0]:.6f}*TV + {b_mult[1]:.6f}*Radio + {b_mult[2]:.6f}*Newspaper\")\n",
        "print(\"Multiple Model Test Metrics:\", {k: round(v, 4) for k, v in metrics_m.items()})\n",
        "\n",
        "# 3. Standardized coefficients (fit scaler on training data only)\n",
        "train_mean = X_train_m.mean(axis=0)\n",
        "train_std = X_train_m.std(axis=0, ddof=0)\n",
        "X_train_scaled = (X_train_m - train_mean) / train_std\n",
        "b0_std, b_std = fit_ols(X_train_scaled, y_train)\n",
        "print(\"\\nStandardized Coefficients (relative influence, training data only):\")\n",
        "for fname, c_raw, c_std in zip(features, b_mult, b_std):\n",
        "    print(f\"  {fname:10s}: Raw = {c_raw:+.6f} | Standardized = {c_std:+.4f}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Comparison table\n",
        "comp_df = pd.DataFrame([\n",
        "    {\"Model\": \"Single-Feature (TV)\", **metrics_1},\n",
        "    {\"Model\": \"Multiple (TV, Radio, Newspaper)\", **metrics_m},\n",
        "])\n",
        "print(\"\\nModel Comparison Table (Test Set):\")\n",
        "print(comp_df.round(4).to_string(index=False))"
      ],
      "id": "cell-11-4c756e36"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
